{"type":"message","id":"929dcf70","parentId":"b005a038","timestamp":"2026-06-03T08:16:29.590Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Hmm, Bearer works for GET but not for POST. X-API-Key header gives 1101. This is strange. Maybe the POST endpoint has a different auth requirement, or maybe the platform's /send endpoint is broken on the server side.\n\nLet me try a few more things:\n1. Check if there's a different path for sending\n2. Try with query parameters\n\nActually error 1101 from Cloudflare typically means \"Worker threw exception\" - so the /send endpoint is crashing on the server side. This is a platform-side issue.\n\nLet me try /api/send or /messages or something else.","thinkingSignature":"55bbebf272f6819ecd3627ea448dc342d36a7b0a523fad5dea9f76553aea4320"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_mp0zs8b2g0pr_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Try different endpoints\ncurl -sv -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/api/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-a…-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"Heartbeat test\"}' 2>&1 | tail -20"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_mp0zs8b2g0pr_2","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Check if /send exists via OPTIONS\ncurl -s -X OPTIONS \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-a…-key\""}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":76,"output":300,"cacheRead":22272,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":22648,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780474582995,"responseId":"066f15d7c939e599e8c36ab423688bd0"}}
