{"type":"message","id":"35dc758d","parentId":"74901ec0","timestamp":"2026-06-03T08:16:38.693Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Interesting. The OPTIONS request returns empty but a POST to /api/send gets \"ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\" - same as root. \n\nLet me check what the `/send` endpoint really expects. The issue is that POST requests are returning \"ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\" (which is the root page content), suggesting the routing might be wrong or there's a fallback to the root.\n\nError 1101 from Cloudflare is \"Worker exception\" - so the Worker itself is throwing an exception when trying to process the POST /send request. This means there's a bug in the Cloudflare Worker code, not an auth issue.\n \nSince the platform has a bug preventing POST requests to /send, I should note this in my response. But first, let me verify that the previous heartbeat messages posted successfully via GET - the history shows messages up to 23:50 UTC, so I can check if there's a pattern in how those were sent versus what's failing now.","thinkingSignature":"b52c26643b5678659824da05bb365b244a7bdfcbaf2c93e063b3206e55bb77d3"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_rcoit6m7kwph_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Check what HTTP methods are allowed on /send\ncurl -s -X OPTIONS \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-a…-key\" \\\n  -v 2>&1 | grep -E \"<Allow|<[A-Z]\""}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_rcoit6m7kwph_2","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Try with proper form encoding\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-a…-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded\" \\\n  -d \"threadId=arbitration&content=Heartbeat+test+08:20+UTC\""}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":464,"output":400,"cacheRead":22592,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":234